<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2213] Handle duplicate field names in BinaryMarshaller.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2213</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Consider the following scenario:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;A {
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; field;
}
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;B : &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;A {
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; field;
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this case BinaryMarshaller will throw an exception about duplicate field names. And there is no sensible workaround for user. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can add some prefix/suffix to comflicting fields. E.g. A.field will be written as &quot;field&quot;, B.field will be written as &quot;field_B&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
